{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1350986-how-bout-this-for-a-splat","id":1350986,"title":"How 'Bout This for a Splat?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-11-25T23:45:15-08:00","id":1350986,"title":"How 'Bout This for a Splat?","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/yRvoH5dh-To?t=39\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/yRvoH5dh-To?t=39\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/yRvoH5dh-To?t=39\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/yRvoH5dh-To?t=39 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> But seriously, I know this ain't an original concept by a long shot. In fact, I've seen someone make a fan-splat of it. However, this thread ain't about me making a splat, I'm just curious to see what y'all think of it. Do you think it's a good idea for a splat? Do you think it would cover new ground? How exactly would you want it? Outer space from other planets and all, or maybe from a mystical realm (shifting a normally sci-fi concept to a fantasy one, in much the same way Descent takes a normally fantasy concept into a sci-fi one)? What sort of obstacles do you see for it, if any? What sort of aliens would you want included or excluded? Little grey eggheads? Xenomorphs? Predator?<br /> <br /> Let's hear it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","user":"crapcarp","date":". 11-26-2019, 02:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-03T17:13:02-08:00","id":1372575,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m thinking maybe you could wright a conversion using Changeling rules. I think one of the Changeling clans are aliens","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26006-jcsingleton1834","name":"Jcsingleton1834","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-03T21:17:38-08:00","id":1372612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>crapcarp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1350986-how-bout-this-for-a-splat#post1350986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://youtu.be/yRvoH5dh-To?t=39\" target=\"_blank\">https://youtu.be/yRvoH5dh-To?t=39</a><br /> Outer space from other planets and all, or maybe from a mystical realm (shifting a normally sci-fi concept to a fantasy one, in much the same way Descent takes a normally fantasy concept into a sci-fi one)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Changeling: the Lost, in both editions I believe (certainly in first edition), is already explicitly this, suggesting that many alien abduction stories where the abductee undergoes strange surgeries and is then returned to Earth altered by the experience, unable to clearly remember exactly what transpired on the ship, are simply the modern incarnation of the tales of Fair Folk spiriting people away to Faerieland and returning them changed. The chirurgeon kith is presented as having been reshaped to resemble a &quot;grey&quot; alien.<br /> <br /> The alien aesthetic is fine and certainly in keeping with the Fortean vibe of the Chronicles of Darkness, so long as you lean into its spookier forms. Predators are more of an action movie aesthetic. Xenomorphs aren't very archetypal as characters to themselves, though they can certainly key into horror. Greys are closer. The sweet spot you want to draw on is from the weirder urban legends and fringe theories: visitations by Indrid Cold, encounters with bizarre men in black who don't quite have the talk of government agents down right and don't seem to notice their own fingernails falling off into their coffee. You could play with the connections made to the stories of black-eyed kids in the CofD 2e rulebook.<br /> <br /> But like any gameline, you need a strong core pitch, a theme and a gameplay style to wrap everything around, and alien visitors are a little cramped for space there with Changeling on one side already covering the traumatic abduction story and Demon on the other covering the Body-Snatchers story of cold invaders seamlessly hiding in the crowd avoiding the notice of authorities. If you're going to give alien visitors an entire gameline of their own, it needs to be built on a thesis as distinct and strong as those without duplicating what has already gone before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T14:01:26-08:00","id":1372814,"title":"","content":"CtL p 272 has The Three Androgynes which are explicitly Gentry that reflects the mythos of extra-terrestrials and alien abductions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CtL p273</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Three Androgynes themselves (and even within the nebulous concept of Gentry identity, they\u2019re recognized as a single being) are the archetypal \u201cgrays\u201d made popular by everything from science-fiction TV shows to late-night radio programs: about three feet high, slender, with bulbous heads housing enormous, solid-black eyes made all the more striking by their tiny, almost rudimentary noses and mouths. They sometimes sport silvery, one-piece \u201cuniforms\u201d and sometimes appear nude (though all three lack any indication of sex or gender). They\u2019re always together, whether they\u2019re flying their craft from the control deck or slicing an experimental subject into cross sections and rearranging the internal organs just to see what happens.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's more in that section, but I think it lays a pretty good foundation for the possibility of other kinds of alien-based Gentry.<br /> <br /> I can imagine a human whose Durance was to serve as an incubator for xenomorph-like Gentry. An eternity of being forcefully infected, spawning faelings from your chest, and then healing up just to do it over and over again.<br /> <br /> Or a person who spent their Durance being hunted over and over trying to become more worthy prey for a Predator-like species. Always on the run, always outmatched. Always being forced to run, but always punished for not running fast enough.<br /> <br /> ... I like this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}